The HC-SR501 output is a digital signal. Its HIGH output is suitable for an Arduino Uno digital input. This answer assumes the buzzer is an active buzzer module with its own input circuitry, not a bare two-pin buzzer.

```cpp
const int pirPin = 2;
const int buzzerPin = 9;

void setup() {
  pinMode(pirPin, INPUT);
  pinMode(buzzerPin, OUTPUT);
  digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);
}

void loop() {
  int motion = digitalRead(pirPin);

  if (motion == HIGH) {
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);
  }
}
```

No extra component is needed for the specified active buzzer module. If the part is actually a bare buzzer rather than a module, its current requirement must be checked before driving it directly from an Uno GPIO.

